[EXAMPLES]
overview: Real-world examples of documentation updates
purpose: Show how to apply self-learning process

[EXAMPLE_1_USER_EXPLICIT_RULE]
scenario: User says "Never use std::regex in core, too slow"

step_1: Identify
  - This is from user (meets CRITERIA_1)
  - It's a constraint/rule
  - Target: CONSTRAINTS.toon

step_2: Locate
  - Open docs/agent/CONSTRAINTS.toon
  - Find appropriate place (alphabetical? at end? ask yourself)
  - Add as [CONSTRAINT_N]

step_3: Check duplicate
  - Search CONSTRAINTS.toon for "regex"
  - Not found, proceed

step_4: Write
  [CONSTRAINT_12]
  rule: Never use std::regex in core (performance critical)
  why: Regex engine is slow, unacceptable latency for Layer 5
  alternatives: Use simple string matching or hand-written parser
  enforcement: Code review veto if found

step_5: Edit
  Use Edit tool to add to CONSTRAINTS.toon

step_6: Verify
  - File structure intact
  - No syntax errors
  - Constraint is clear

step_7: Commit
  git commit -m "docs: [constraint] add regex prohibition

  Source: User explicitly stated in work session
  File: docs/agent/CONSTRAINTS.toon

  Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"

[EXAMPLE_2_FOUND_IN_CODE]
scenario: Reading core_engine.cpp, found comment: "Key rotation happens every 30 days"

step_1: Identify
  - Found in code with comment (meets CRITERIA_2)
  - It's cryptographic detail
  - Target: CRYPTO.toon

step_2: Locate
  - Open docs/agent/CRYPTO.toon
  - Find [KEY_HIERARCHY] or [NONCE_HANDLING] section
  - Add details there

step_3: Check duplicate
  - Search "rotation" in CRYPTO.toon
  - Not found, proceed

step_4: Write
  In [KEY_HIERARCHY] section:
  rotation_interval: 30 days
  implementation: Timer in identity_engine.cpp (line 142)
  mechanism: Generates new Device Key, updates via signed Roster
  verification: See KEY-MANAGEMENT-DESIGN.md for full details

step_5: Edit
  Update CRYPTO.toon with rotation details

step_6: Verify
  - New info integrates with existing KEY_HIERARCHY section
  - References actual code location
  - Clear and concise

step_7: Commit
  git commit -m "docs: [crypto] document key rotation interval

  Source: Code inspection, core_engine.cpp line 142
  File: docs/agent/CRYPTO.toon

  Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"

[EXAMPLE_3_DISCOVERED_ARCHITECTURE]
scenario: While debugging found: relay_session reuses QUIC connections

step_1: Identify
  - Discovered from code analysis (meets CRITERIA_3)
  - It's architectural pattern
  - Target: MODULES.toon or ARCHITECTURE.toon (connection reuse pattern)

step_2: Locate
  - Open docs/agent/MODULES.toon
  - Find [MODULE.RELAY] section
  - Add subsection about connection reuse

step_3: Check duplicate
  - Search "reuse" in MODULES.toon and ARCHITECTURE.toon
  - Found in ARCHITECTURE.toon Level 5, but no relay details
  - Proceed (will complement existing info)

step_4: Write
  In [MODULE.RELAY] section, add:
  connection_reuse: true
  mechanism: QUIC connection pooled per peer, reused for sequential messages
  benefit: Reduce handshake overhead, improve throughput
  implementation: See relay_session.cpp (refactored in EPIC-18)
  verification: Confirmed via code walk-through

step_5: Edit
  Update MODULES.toon relay section

step_6: Verify
  - Doesn't duplicate ARCHITECTURE.toon
  - Adds relay-specific details
  - References implementation

step_7: Commit
  git commit -m "docs: [module] document relay connection reuse

  Source: Code discovery while analyzing relay_session.cpp
  File: docs/agent/MODULES.toon

  Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"

[EXAMPLE_4_FIXING_ERROR]
scenario: ACTIVE_EPICS.toon says EPIC-10 is "IN_PROGRESS" but code shows it's complete

step_1: Identify
  - Found error in docs (meets CRITERIA_4)
  - Target: ACTIVE_EPICS.toon (status update)

step_2: Locate
  - Open docs/agent/ACTIVE_EPICS.toon
  - Find [EPIC_10_TRANSPORT_ROUTING] section

step_3: Check duplicate
  - This is the only entry for EPIC-10
  - Proceed

step_4: Write
  Change:
    status: IN_PROGRESS 🔴
  To:
    status: COMPLETED ✅
  And update description to reflect completion

step_5: Edit
  Update ACTIVE_EPICS.toon

step_6: Verify
  - Status matches code reality
  - Other epics that depend on EPIC-10 can now be unblocked
  - Links to deliverables still valid

step_7: Commit
  git commit -m "docs: [epic] mark EPIC-10 as completed

  Source: Code verification, all deliverables present in mirage-core/
  File: docs/agent/ACTIVE_EPICS.toon

  Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"

[WHAT_TO_AVOID]
example_bad_1: Too vague
  "The system is complex"
  problem: No actionable information

example_bad_2: Speculation
  "Probably the developers meant to implement it this way"
  problem: Vague, unverified

example_bad_3: Opinion
  "This would be better if implemented differently"
  problem: Not a rule, just preference

example_bad_4: Obvious
  "The code iterates through elements"
  problem: Anyone reading code sees this

example_bad_5: Implementation detail
  "Vector grows by 2x when capacity exceeded"
  problem: Can change, not architectural rule

[KEY_TAKEAWAYS]
✅ Small targeted updates (5-10 lines)
✅ One file per update (don't scatter info)
✅ Always verify source (code review or user confirmation)
✅ Link to references (line numbers, existing docs)
✅ Clear commit message with source attribution
✅ Check for duplicates before adding

❌ Large multi-concept updates
❌ Speculative or opinion-based info
❌ Obvious facts from code
❌ Without source attribution
❌ Breaking existing structure/format
❌ Forgetting to commit [docs] prefix
